Chapter 2
Operating income at different levels; targets and income taxes
الربح التشغيلي عند مستويات مختلفة والأهداف وأثر الضريبة
Chapter 1 found the point at which Orontes earns nothing. This chapter asks what it earns everywhere else. Once the contribution margin and the fixed costs are known, the operating income at any volume is a single multiplication and a single subtraction, and a whole schedule of outcomes can be produced in a few minutes.
The chapter then adds the complication the exam uses to separate careful candidates from quick ones: income taxes. A target stated as operating income and the same target stated as net income are different questions, and the second has to be converted before the first formula will work.
Figure F702-01 is your map.
Figure F702-01. Chapter 2 roadmap: income at any level, drawn, targeted, and taxed.
